  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Each of the six letters A, B, C, D, E and F stand for a different digit from 1 to 9. Find the value of\n\n$$(AB)\\times(CD)\\times(EF)$$\n\nthat is as close as possible to $30\\,000$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p12-q7-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "29\\,988",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p12-q7-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "For example, 17 × 28 × 63; the difference from 30 000 is 12.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Here $AB$, $CD$ and $EF$ are two-digit numbers. One valid choice uses the six distinct digits $1,7,2,8,6,3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}17\\times28\\times63&=476\\times63\\\\17\\times28\\times63&=29\\,988\\\\30\\,000-29\\,988&=12\\end{align*}$$\n\nTo check optimality, list the possible two-digit numbers using different nonzero digits. Check triples in increasing order, retaining only triples whose six digits are all different. The $10\\,080$ unordered valid triples have minimum distance $12$ from $30\\,000$. Both $17\\times28\\times63$ and $17\\times36\\times49$ give $29\\,988$, so this is the closest value.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
